{
  "_note": [
    "F3-1 golden vectors: the PINNED ERC-8128 wire format plus the two",
    "legacy variants the verifier stays tolerant of. Single source for the",
    "conformance suites: mcp_server (pytest, tests/test_erc8128_conformance.py),",
    "em-plugin-sdk (tests/test_erc8128.py), sdk/python (tests/test_signer.py),",
    "sdk/typescript (src/__tests__/erc8128.conformance.test.ts) and",
    "ows-mcp-server (src/erc8128-base.test.ts) — the TS runtimes joined in F3-2.",
    "Signatures are deterministic (RFC 6979): the same key + signature base",
    "produces the same 65 bytes in eth_account and ethers, so every",
    "implementation of a given variant must reproduce these headers exactly.",
    "private_key is stored WITHOUT the 0x prefix (the pre-commit secret",
    "scanner blocks any literal 0x + 64 hex chars); loaders re-prefix it.",
    "It is a synthetic test key (0x42 * 32) that never held funds."
  ],
  "policy": {
    "pinned_wire_format": {
      "decided": "2026-08-01 (F3-1)",
      "alg": "eip191",
      "alg_required": true,
      "keyid_lowercase": true,
      "keyid_format": "erc8128:{chain_id}:{address_lowercase}",
      "label": "eth",
      "signature_params_order": [
        "created",
        "expires",
        "nonce",
        "keyid",
        "alg"
      ],
      "covered_components_order": [
        "@method",
        "@authority",
        "@path",
        "@query (only when the URL has a query string)",
        "content-digest (only when the request has a body)"
      ],
      "signature_encoding": "base64(r||s||v, 65 bytes) wrapped in RFC 8941 byte sequence",
      "content_digest": "sha-256 (RFC 9530)",
      "signing": "EIP-191 personal_sign over the RFC 9421 signature base",
      "rationale": [
        "alg=eip191 + lowercase keyid is what the canonical skill",
        "(dashboard/public/skill.md v10.0.0 EM8128Client) documents and what",
        "the external fleet already emits \u2014 the copies we cannot migrate by",
        "PR. F3-2 converged the 5 client copies to canonical; the backend",
        "reference signer (server-side test helper) still emits",
        "legacy_no_alg \u2014 see the implementations map.",
        "Lowercase keyid is mandatory: the checksummed-keyid drift caused",
        "the v9.x silent-auth-failure INC (sdk/python/_signer.py:210-213)."
      ]
    },
    "verifier_tolerance": {
      "accepts_missing_alg": true,
      "accepts_checksummed_keyid": true,
      "note": [
        "The backend verifier deliberately stays tolerant of both legacy",
        "variants (it rebuilds the byte-exact base the client signed and",
        "lowercases both sides of the address comparison). Do NOT harden",
        "acceptance until every emitter passes the canonical vector; a",
        "hardening is a contract change: update these vectors, the",
        "conformance suite, and bump skill.md."
      ]
    }
  },
